  <h1>Ultimate Popover Solution</h1>

  <p>Are you the fan of components plug & play? Those ones you just add and magically works. We gonna explroe one of the
    msot popular today!</p>

  <h2>What's wrong with currently used popovers?</h2>
  <p>Isn't it crazy how much JavaScript a popover/tooltip implementaiton requires and yet still might fail when trigger
    moves around or dissapears. In almost every applciaiton there is always a case where popvoer is cut by the
    screen/parent.
    On the top of that tooltip contributes in non-trivial way to web applictions speed. Don't elive such a tiny detai
    lcan imapct performance? YOu can checkout react devtools to see how much time is spend on rendering just tooltips
    and claculatign their position. I'm not even gonna elaborate on more ca;culatio nregarding that little arrow poting
    at tooltip/popvoer trigger. Today we are about to put stop to this misery.</p>


  <a-h2 content="Enter Ultimate Popover" />
  <p>New popover API arrived, it's baseline 2024 newly available. It can be used for tooltips, popovers and modals as
    well! It leverages the power of CSS and HTML to provide stunning user experience without the need for JavaScript
    libraries. Lack of Javascript allows your business logic to do not compete with tooltip implementation for computing
    power of single tthreaded JS.</p>

  <p>That's all sound good but... creating a popover is not that trivial even with new API, you have to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Be aware of containging block & inset-modified containing block to know how to correctly position popover</li>
    <li>Ensure the trigger can be used as popover anchor(or anchors!). They both have to live in same containg block and
      same DOM tree</li>
    <li>Handle variosu edges cases especially with styling the border.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>That's why today we gonna take a look at implementation that should work in (almost) all cases.</p>

  <h2>tl;dr if you wanna just code, copy CSS below and take a look how html example looks like.</h2>


  <p>You staying here means curiosity has won today! Let's dive!</p>

  <h3>Firstly, browser popover API</h3>
  <p>We have received plenty of new toys to play with.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>Popover</code>- an attribute on popover to indicate the behaviour. Three valeus allowed
      <code>auto</code>(default), <code>hint</code> and <code>manual</code>. First two can dismisse popover by clicking
      outside the popvoer area or pressing Esc. General difference is that openign popvoer with type auto closes other
      popover with type auto and similar with type <code>hint</code> which closes other popvoer with type
      <code>hint</code>, unless popvoers are nested!. <a
        href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Global_attributes/popover">Read more on
        MDN.</a>
    </li>
  </ul>


